M3.1 — exact/regex/path surfaces (commit 727814a)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
Before: RepositoryIndex::exact()/regex() had NO production caller (the
index fed path candidates only) — the M3.1 reset's "capability landed"
note was unprovable.
- TaskIndex::query_exact/query_regex: bounded direct surfaces over the
  indexed corpus (path-ordered hits with line+snippet; invalid regex =
  typed IndexError, never a panic); query_paths via RepositoryIndex::path.
- context.query gains mode=fused|exact|regex|path (default then: fused).
  All direct modes refresh from the change journal first (reasons
  exact_query/regex_query/path_query) and record retrieval evidence
  (MOD-CTX-001) — path-mode string hits included.
- Proofs: unit exact_regex_and_path_surfaces_answer_from_the_live_index
  (line-anchored hits, typed regex errors, incremental delta tracked,
  bounds hold); daemon E2E turns c5/c6 — exact + regex through the REAL
  daemon against content created mid-run by change.apply.
- MUTATION CHECK: regex surface disabled (empty hits) — first attempt
  PASSED (the assertion matched the mode label, not real hits); the
  assertion was hardened to require the body-line snippet
  ("snippet":"true" — a line appearing nowhere else in the conversation)
  and the mutation then FAILED the E2E as required. The false-pass and
  its fix are recorded here deliberately.

M3.7 — planner-routed auto mode (second commit)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
Before: modbit_context::planner (L0-L3 classification, REQ ledger
EV-0001) was logic-only with zero production callers.
- TaskIndexWriter::query_auto: REAL index signals (bounded exact probe
  over the live corpus, symbol-defined check, term count, structural /
  engineering phrasing) → planner::plan → route to the MINIMUM
  sufficient level:
    L0 Exact          → exact surface
    L1 Hybrid         → fused (BM25+path+symbol)
    L2 Structural     → symbol defs/refs (single defined identifier) or
                        fused with structural marker
    L3 Engineering    → fused ×2 + an explicit note that the full
                        evidence graph (Git/diagnostics/runtime) lands
                        with M3.6
  The plan (level, rationale, signals) rides EVERY auto response as
  routing provenance. auto is now the tool default; explicit modes
  unchanged. (docs/18: LLM rerank is optional and NOT required for P0 —
  rerank.rs stays unwired.)
- Proofs (daemon E2E, 9 scripted turns, MODBIT_MAX_TURNS=16):
  multi-term → level hybrid (auto:hybrid); "definition of X" → level
  structural (auto:structural:fused); bare defined identifier → level
  exact (auto:exact — NO over-escalation, the REQ-EV-0001 core);
  "How does the retry flow work" → level engineering
  (auto:engineering:fused) with the M3.6 note — all asserted in the
  DURABLE conversation of a REAL daemon run.
- One honest test iteration: the first c7 expectation assumed a bare
  identifier routes to structural; the planner correctly chose the
  cheaper L0-exact (minimum sufficient level). The TEST was fixed, not
  the planner.
- MUTATION CHECK: planner bypassed (all queries forced hybrid) → the
  structural/engineering/exact routing assertions FAILED (the dump shows
  every turn answered "level":"hybrid","rationale":"mutated"). REVERTED;
  post-revert E2E green.

